{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017vVtt4LSSJwT6c44WdJPnM","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FAQ - EMNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/\"},{\"title\":\"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)\",\"url\":\"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 (@emnlpmeeting) · X\",\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/emnlpmeeting\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 (@emnlpmeeting) / Posts / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/emnlpmeeting\"},{\"title\":\"[EMNLP 2025] First Call for Papers | ACL Member Portal\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/emnlp-2025-first-call-papers\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about EMNLP 2026 and the review process:\n\nEMNLP 2026 will use ACL Rolling Review (ARR) as a reviewing system, but final decisions will be made by the conference. Both submissions of articles for review and commitment of reviewed articles to the conference will be performed via the Open Review platform, with authors following a two-step process where they first submit articles to ARR for reviews and meta-reviews, then commit their reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026.\n\nRegarding reviewer deadlines, if you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews - by July 29.\n\nHowever, the search results do not contain specific details about the EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines document or review form itself. The results reference the ARR (ACL Rolling Review) system and general procedures, but don't include direct links to or content from the actual reviewer guidelines or review form template for EMNLP 2026. You may want to check the official EMNLP 2026 website (2026.emnlp.org) or the ACL Rolling Review website (aclrollingreview.org) directly for the complete reviewer guidelines and review form template.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"352b5339-5de3-432c-8453-cee5bd2f497d","uuid":"09342514-4fd1-4aac-8e00-8d5dcdb1ef9f","timestamp":"2026-05-16T11:55:15.186Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01FcmyeL1owocRupcaNaz6ZX","content":[{"title":"FAQ - EMNLP 2026","url":"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/"},{"title":"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)","url":"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N","url":"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026"},{"title":"EMNLP | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 (@emnlpmeeting) · X","url":"https://twitter.com/emnlpmeeting"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 (@emnlpmeeting) / Posts / X","url":"https://x.com/emnlpmeeting"},{"title":"[EMNLP 2025] First Call for Papers | ACL Member Portal","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/emnlp-2025-first-call-papers"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about EMNLP 2026 and the review process:\n\nEMNLP 2026 will use ACL Rolling Review (ARR) as a reviewing system, but final decisions will be made by the conference. Both submissions of articles for review and commitment of reviewed articles to the conference will be performed via the Open Review platform, with authors following a two-step process where they first submit articles to ARR for reviews and meta-reviews, then commit their reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026.\n\nRegarding reviewer deadlines, if you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews - by July 29.\n\nHowever, the search results do not contain specific details about the EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines document or review form itself. The results reference the ARR (ACL Rolling Review) system and general procedures, but don't include direct links to or content from the actual reviewer guidelines or review form template for EMNLP 2026. You may want to check the official EMNLP 2026 website (2026.emnlp.org) or the ACL Rolling Review website (aclrollingreview.org) directly for the complete reviewer guidelines and review form template."],"durationSeconds":6.409424326}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H99BBV82uNhdmizvHuwJE1","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2025 review form scoring criteria dimensions\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"NAACL-HLT 2021 Instructions for Reviewers - EMNLP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/emnlp-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"Automatically Measuring Peer Review's Utility for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.1476.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"Conference Decisions · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://gist.github.com/antonisa/2158dee79179c7c49304ef353887bfa0\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2025 Peer Review FAQ\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2025/PeerReviewFAQ\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"‭ACL Peer Review Committee Report‬\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/images/d/d3/ACL_Peer_Review_Committee_Report2_Incentives_May_2025.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, here's what I found about the EMNLP 2025 review form scoring criteria:\n\n## Scoring Scale\n\nEMNLP 2025 uses a 5 point scale with half point increments, similar to ACL 2020.\n\n## Main Review Dimensions\n\nThe review form consists of four main sections, with the \"In-Depth Review\" section designed for overall assessment of the paper and to provide evidence to support opinions, which includes three subsections: The core review.\n\n## Key Scoring Areas\n\nThe reviews assess papers across several dimensions:\n\n1. **Soundness and Reproducibility**: Reviewers answer questions like \"How do you rate the paper's reproducibility?\" and \"Will members of the ACL community be able to reproduce or verify the results in this paper?\" using scores of 1-5.\n\n2. **Overall Assessment Scoring**: A rating of 3 (ambivalent) is allowed, and reviewers are encouraged to take a stand on whether the paper is above or below the borderline by selecting 2.5 or 3.5, though a score of 3 may be used if the paper is borderline or the reviewer cannot decide.\n\n3. **Evaluation Criteria**: The main criteria for Findings papers are soundness and reproducibility, while conference recommendations may also consider novelty, impact and other factors.\n\nFor more detailed explanations of each scoring level, detailed explanations for each point level are provided in the review form itself.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"352b5339-5de3-432c-8453-cee5bd2f497d","uuid":"19767dde-615a-435e-aca9-f2ca73dd24af","timestamp":"2026-05-16T11:55:15.820Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2025 review form scoring criteria dimensions","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015YLoJRSyp1KPrjALVjdopM","content":[{"title":"NAACL-HLT 2021 Instructions for Reviewers - EMNLP 2025","url":"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/emnlp-2025-statistics/"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"Automatically Measuring Peer Review's Utility for Authors","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.emnlp-main.1476.pdf"},{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"EMNLP Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/"},{"title":"Conference Decisions · GitHub","url":"https://gist.github.com/antonisa/2158dee79179c7c49304ef353887bfa0"},{"title":"ICML 2025 Peer Review FAQ","url":"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2025/PeerReviewFAQ"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"‭ACL Peer Review Committee Report‬","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/images/d/d3/ACL_Peer_Review_Committee_Report2_Incentives_May_2025.pdf"}]},"Based on my search results, here's what I found about the EMNLP 2025 review form scoring criteria:\n\n## Scoring Scale\n\nEMNLP 2025 uses a 5 point scale with half point increments, similar to ACL 2020.\n\n## Main Review Dimensions\n\nThe review form consists of four main sections, with the \"In-Depth Review\" section designed for overall assessment of the paper and to provide evidence to support opinions, which includes three subsections: The core review.\n\n## Key Scoring Areas\n\nThe reviews assess papers across several dimensions:\n\n1. **Soundness and Reproducibility**: Reviewers answer questions like \"How do you rate the paper's reproducibility?\" and \"Will members of the ACL community be able to reproduce or verify the results in this paper?\" using scores of 1-5.\n\n2. **Overall Assessment Scoring**: A rating of 3 (ambivalent) is allowed, and reviewers are encouraged to take a stand on whether the paper is above or below the borderline by selecting 2.5 or 3.5, though a score of 3 may be used if the paper is borderline or the reviewer cannot decide.\n\n3. **Evaluation Criteria**: The main criteria for Findings papers are soundness and reproducibility, while conference recommendations may also consider novelty, impact and other factors.\n\nFor more detailed explanations of each scoring level, detailed explanations for each point level are provided in the review form itself."],"durationSeconds":6.958953555}}
