{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012tjQ7CiUUtD156PXD4F681","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review review form 2025 2026 overall assessment scoring scale dimensions\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection\",\"url\":\"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Dashboard\",\"url\":\"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review assessment scoring:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nThe search results indicate these are the key scoring dimensions for the review form, though the specific scale details for each dimension aren't fully detailed in the available results. The results show that the soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review.\n\nThe results also mention that if your overall assessment for this paper is either 'Consider for award' or 'Borderline award', please briefly describe why, indicating some of the possible values for the overall assessment field.\n\nIf you need more specific details about the exact numerical scale (e.g., 1-5 points) or additional dimensions beyond these three scores, you may want to visit the official ACL Rolling Review review form directly at aclrollingreview.org/reviewform.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"352b5339-5de3-432c-8453-cee5bd2f497d","uuid":"4244e7e3-91d3-465f-ba89-683568b18767","timestamp":"2026-05-16T11:55:24.474Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review review form 2025 2026 overall assessment scoring scale dimensions","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01LcRnW4qpTvWyTC6JBxATM6","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection","url":"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/"},{"title":"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"ARR Dashboard","url":"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \"Publish or Perish\" Circus | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review assessment scoring:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nThe search results indicate these are the key scoring dimensions for the review form, though the specific scale details for each dimension aren't fully detailed in the available results. The results show that the soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review.\n\nThe results also mention that if your overall assessment for this paper is either 'Consider for award' or 'Borderline award', please briefly describe why, indicating some of the possible values for the overall assessment field.\n\nIf you need more specific details about the exact numerical scale (e.g., 1-5 points) or additional dimensions beyond these three scores, you may want to visit the official ACL Rolling Review review form directly at aclrollingreview.org/reviewform."],"durationSeconds":4.909656353999996}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014tfgSaGyGyw2Jp2xomjLkq","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform scoring criteria overall assessment\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Response to ACL 2023 Questions\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/ACL-2023-session/\"},{\"title\":\"Action Editor Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/actioneditorform\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"Area Keywords at ARR\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/areas\"},{\"title\":\"ARR SAC Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/sacguidelines\"}]\n\nThe search results show information about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) scoring criteria and overall assessment form. Here's what I found:\n\n## Scoring Criteria\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n## Additional Assessment Details\n\nFor the \"Main vs Findings papers,\" the main criteria for Findings are soundness and reproducibility. Conference recommendations may also consider novelty, impact and other factors.\n\n## Overall Assessment Scale\n\nThe form includes recommendation levels such as:\n- 5 = Consider for Award: I think this paper could be considered for an outstanding paper award at an *ACL conference (up to top 2.5% papers).\n- 2 = Resubmit next cycle: I think this paper needs substantial revisions that can be completed by the next ARR cycle. 1.5 = Resubmit after next cycle: I think this paper needs substantial revisions that cannot be completed by the next ARR cycle. 1 = Do not resubmit: This paper has to be fully redone, or it is not relevant to the *ACL community\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"352b5339-5de3-432c-8453-cee5bd2f497d","uuid":"0acacb60-fdfd-4a63-8020-c1378f1e5436","timestamp":"2026-05-16T11:55:26.861Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform scoring criteria overall assessment","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01CZ16B5qydGWDtUfu97cFtN","content":[{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"Response to ACL 2023 Questions","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/ACL-2023-session/"},{"title":"Action Editor Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/actioneditorform"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"Area Keywords at ARR","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/areas"},{"title":"ARR SAC Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/sacguidelines"}]},"The search results show information about the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) scoring criteria and overall assessment form. Here's what I found:\n\n## Scoring Criteria\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n## Additional Assessment Details\n\nFor the \"Main vs Findings papers,\" the main criteria for Findings are soundness and reproducibility. Conference recommendations may also consider novelty, impact and other factors.\n\n## Overall Assessment Scale\n\nThe form includes recommendation levels such as:\n- 5 = Consider for Award: I think this paper could be considered for an outstanding paper award at an *ACL conference (up to top 2.5% papers).\n- 2 = Resubmit next cycle: I think this paper needs substantial revisions that can be completed by the next ARR cycle. 1.5 = Resubmit after next cycle: I think this paper needs substantial revisions that cannot be completed by the next ARR cycle. 1 = Do not resubmit: This paper has to be fully redone, or it is not relevant to the *ACL community"],"durationSeconds":6.7703085729999986}}
