{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HhUX13uUnc84FqR97dvBXe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the complete ARR/EMNLP review form. Let me also check for EMNLP acceptance rate information.\n\nKey scoring dimensions for my review:\n- **Soundness**: 1-5 (half-point increments)\n- **Excitement**: 1-5 (half-point increments)\n- **Overall Assessment**: 1-5 (half-point increments), where 4 = Conference, 3 = Findings, 5 = Award\n- **Confidence**: 1-5\n- **Reproducibility**: 1-5\n\nNow I need to dispatch two reviewers:\n\n\n- R1 will focus on methods and experiments\n- R2 will focus on novelty and related work\n\nThen I'll conduct the roundtable discussion. Let me launch both reviewer agents in parallel and record the key paper details: the title is \"Strong Predictors, Weak Selectors: Why Confidence Signals Cannot Scale Structured Information Extraction,\" with a dual contribution showing that confidence signals can predict quality (AUROC 0.82, ρ 0.44) but fail at best-of-N selection due to multi-causal failures including instance degeneracy.\n\nNow I'm mapping the experimental setup to validate which experiments are actually present in the paper—checking that the LLaMA-3.1-8B results on CoNLL appear in Tables 2 and 3, and the trained verifier baseline with logistic regression on 5 signals appears in Table 4.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1284,"cache_read_input_tokens":53765,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1284},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"352b5339-5de3-432c-8453-cee5bd2f497d","uuid":"166357e0-5d1e-452e-bb9b-408df921cf07"}
